Fixed Drug Eruption (FDE) patients typically present with pinkish papules turning brownish with purpuric edges but lack the deep violaceous pigment seen here. Morbilliform Drug Eruption (MDE) involves multisystem purpuric symptoms and cop Judiciary, which are not mentioned. Erythema migrans is associated with erythema and beta-blockers but does not match the purpuric skin description. Given the purpuric pigment and drug exposure (including NSAIDs), the most likely diagnosis is **Steven Johnson Syndrome**.

\boxed{B}

